  "steps": [
    "Put the chicken breasts in a saucepan and cover with cold water. Add the salt, bring to a gentle simmer, then cook for 12–15 minutes until the chicken is opaque throughout and cooked through.",
    "Lift the chicken onto a plate and leave it to cool for 5 minutes. Shred it into bite-sized pieces using two forks.",
    "In a small bowl, whisk together the lime juice, tamari, sesame oil, vegetable oil, brown sugar, grated garlic, grated ginger and sliced chilli until the sugar dissolves.",
    "Put the shredded red cabbage, carrot, cucumber and spring onions in a large bowl. Add the shredded chicken, mint and coriander.",
    "Pour over the dressing and toss thoroughly for 1–2 minutes, until the cabbage starts to soften slightly and everything is glossy and evenly coated.",
    "Taste and adjust with a little extra lime juice or salt if needed. Serve topped with the chopped peanuts."
